            "review_title": "Review at Co Ngu Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Robert S\nNew York City, New York3 contributions\n0\nVery good meal! Attractive courtyard!\nFeb 2015 • Solo\nI stayed down the street from this restaurant so I stumbled on it. I ordered spring rolls, octopus salad, crispy duck in orange sauce, a fruit dessert, 2 Heinekens, and a bottle water...all that for 375,000 VD...which to me is very cheap as I live in New York City!\nSpring rolls were fried lightly like they should be.\nOctopus Salad was refreshing and tasty.\nCrispy Duck was amazing!!!\nWaiters don't speak much English which would help them since there are numerous hotels in area but I managed as did he. It was Tet so the establishment was slow but I did not mind and had a fantastic meal! If you are in District 3 I recommend this restaurant!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 3, 2015",
