            "review_title": "Review at Co Ngu Restaurant",
            "review_text": "jackdash\nGeneva, New York61 contributions\n0\nLovely find, caters to Vietnamese\nSep 2012\nWe found this restaurant while looking for another. The attractive courtyard seating and air condtioned colonial building drew us in. We were served by a gentle and attentive young woman, An whose English was very good. We ordered the fried seafood spring rolls, a shredded kholrabi and pork salad (huge plateful and fabulous), delicious and ample morning glory and garlic, rice, and sesame chicken. The latter was nicely cooked and tasty, but we did not taste much sesame. With a cold drink it was $8USD each. Not bad for an elegant atmosphere, good service, and lots of good food.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 10, 2012",
